### PR Summary

Updated the Jenkins Terraform configuration to support separate Docker image tags for DEV and PROD controllers while keeping Jenkins agents on their existing `latest` tag.

### Changes Made
- Added separate `jenkins_docker_tag_dev` and `jenkins_docker_tag_prod` variables for environment-specific controller images.
- Updated `data.tf` to select the appropriate controller image tag based on the deployment environment.
- Added `jenkins_agent_docker_tag` with a default value of `latest` to manage agent images independently.
- Updated `dev.tfvars` and `prod.tfvars` with their respective controller image tags.
- Kept regular Jenkins agents and the SIA scanner agent on the `latest` image tag.
- Preserved the existing Jenkins controller and agent module configurations.

### Expected Outcome
DEV and PROD Jenkins controllers can now be updated independently without requiring changes to the Jenkins agent image tags. This also prevents controller-specific image versions from causing ECR lookup failures for Jenkins agents.
